+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse of what the veterinarian directory answers: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A second page answers it, listing every specialty the clinic knows by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it, all together on one page rather than a page at a time `[REQ-VET-003]`. A veterinarian is shown by full name — first name then last name, as in "Helen Leary". The page lists specialties rather than the roster, so a veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on it. The view is read-only, and who holds which specialty is still not maintained through the application (NG-2). It is reached only by going to it directly; this capability advertises no entry point, so no navigation entry and no link from any other page is part of it.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the specialties the clinic knows, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one of them is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty one or more veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of those veterinarians is shown under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the directory is opened, then all of them are shown together, with nothing offering a further page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by no one rather than omitted.
+2. When the clinic knows no specialties at all, the page opens with an empty list rather than failing.
+3. Specialties are listed in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and so are the veterinarians under each.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#read-models](system-design.md#read-models)  ·  **ADR:** [ADR: Read Models for Page Shapes](adr/2026-08-23-read-models-for-non-entity-page-shapes.md)
+
 ### Language
 
